title: User Journey
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
tags: MermaidExample

A user journey diagram maps the steps a person takes to accomplish a goal, rated by satisfaction score and associated actor. Use it for UX research, customer experience mapping, and service design. Uses `journey`.

---

!! Basic example

```
journey
    title Morning routine
    section Wake up
        Make coffee: 5: Me
        Have breakfast: 3: Me
    section Commute
        Drive to work: 2: Me
        Park the car: 4: Me
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
journey
    title Morning routine
    section Wake up
        Make coffee: 5: Me
        Have breakfast: 3: Me
    section Commute
        Drive to work: 2: Me
        Park the car: 4: Me
$$$

---

!! Real-world example: SaaS product onboarding journey

This example maps a new user's journey from first discovery through active product usage. Sections represent phases of the onboarding funnel; the score (1–5) represents the user's satisfaction at each touchpoint. Multiple actors show which role performs each step.

```
journey
    accTitle: SaaS product onboarding journey
    accDescr: New user journey from discovery to active usage

    %% ── Discovery phase ─────────────────────────
    section Discovery
        Find product via search: 4: Prospect
        Read landing page: 3: Prospect
        Watch demo video: 5: Prospect
        Compare with competitors: 3: Prospect

    %% ── Sign-up phase ────────────────────────────
    section Sign-up
        Click "Start free trial": 5: Prospect
        Complete registration form: 3: Prospect
        Verify email address: 2: Prospect
        Set up profile: 4: New User

    %% ── First login experience ───────────────────
    section First Login
        Follow welcome wizard: 4: New User
        Connect data source: 2: New User, Support
        Create first project: 5: New User
        Invite team member: 4: New User

    %% ── Active usage ─────────────────────────────
    section Active Use
        Run first report: 5: User
        Share results with team: 4: User, Team
        Schedule recurring report: 3: User
        Contact support with question: 2: User, Support

    %% ── Retention ────────────────────────────────
    section Retention
        Receive weekly digest email: 3: User
        Upgrade to paid plan: 5: User
        Recommend to colleague: 5: User
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
journey
    accTitle: SaaS product onboarding journey
    accDescr: New user journey from discovery to active usage

    %% ── Discovery phase ─────────────────────────
    section Discovery
        Find product via search: 4: Prospect
        Read landing page: 3: Prospect
        Watch demo video: 5: Prospect
        Compare with competitors: 3: Prospect

    %% ── Sign-up phase ────────────────────────────
    section Sign-up
        Click "Start free trial": 5: Prospect
        Complete registration form: 3: Prospect
        Verify email address: 2: Prospect
        Set up profile: 4: New User

    %% ── First login experience ───────────────────
    section First Login
        Follow welcome wizard: 4: New User
        Connect data source: 2: New User, Support
        Create first project: 5: New User
        Invite team member: 4: New User

    %% ── Active usage ─────────────────────────────
    section Active Use
        Run first report: 5: User
        Share results with team: 4: User, Team
        Schedule recurring report: 3: User
        Contact support with question: 2: User, Support

    %% ── Retention ────────────────────────────────
    section Retention
        Receive weekly digest email: 3: User
        Upgrade to paid plan: 5: User
        Recommend to colleague: 5: User
$$$

|!Section|!Color|!Meaning|
|Discovery|Blue (1st cycle)|Initial awareness and evaluation phase|
|Sign-up|Green (2nd cycle)|Account creation and verification|
|First Login|Orange (3rd cycle)|Initial product experience and setup|
|Active Use|Pink (4th cycle)|Regular feature engagement|
|Retention|Teal (5th cycle)|Long-term loyalty and advocacy|

---

!! Syntax

```
journey
    title Journey Title
    section Phase One
        Step description: score: Actor1
        Another step: score: Actor1, Actor2
    section Phase Two
        Step: score: Actor2
```

''Score'' is an integer from 1 (very dissatisfied) to 5 (very satisfied). It controls the bar height in the rendered chart.

''Multiple actors'' per step are comma-separated. Each actor gets a distinct color in the actor row.

!! Tips

* Section colors cycle automatically through Mermaid's theme palette — you cannot assign specific hex colors per section (use the legend to map section order to meaning).
* Scores 1–5 map directly to bar height. A score of 3 is neutral; below 3 is a pain point worth improving.
* Multiple actors on a step (e.g. `2: User, Support`) shows a collaborative or hand-off touchpoint.
* Journey diagrams have no `classDef` support — the legend uses text labels and color names rather than hex swatches.
* See also: [[Flowchart]] for process flows, [[Sequence Diagram]] for actor message exchanges.

